{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0443","billNumberShort":"H.B. 443","billNumberLong":"HB0443S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0901","shortTitle":"Amendments to Procedure to Fill A Legislative Vacancy","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"STODDA","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Stoddard, Andrew","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions relating to filling a vacancy in the Legislature.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>requires all vacancies in the Legislature to remain vacant until filled by a special election;<hr><ltbullet>establishes a procedure for calling a special election to fill a vacancy in the Legislature;<hr><ltbullet>describes the dates, which coincide with the dates of other elections, on which a special primary election or a special general election may be held to fill a vacancy in the Legislature;<hr><ltbullet>provides a method for calling a special primary election or a special general election to fill a vacancy in the Legislature on a date other than a date that coincides with the dates of other elections; and<hr><ltbullet>provides for a temporary appointment to fill a vacancy in the Legislature that occurs, or will exist, during a general session of the Legislature, until the vacancy is filled by a special election described in this bill.  ","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Thomas R. Vaughn","fiscalAnalyst":"Ivan D. Djambov","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"OAYKROMLPA","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 14:03:36.587","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"N